  "same_context_judgment": "The actual Per eumdem/eundem Dominum tokens at full-prayer20 are the same masculine accusative singular idem modifying Dominum governed by per. The original raw parse explicitly gives that case/gender/number/lexeme; Allen1903 idem evidence establishes the one class label. Only the private comparator copies receive demonstrative pronoun/adjective. All raw/public part_of_speech nulls remain null. This supplies no generic class inference or other target permission.",
  "same_family_and_person_judgment": "Complete own-source pages168–170 and table818 were actually viewed and read. Source has19 petition tokens plus actual3-token Per eumdem Dominum; target has the same19 petition tokens after finite Genitrice token12, then15-token through-the-same table prefix after idem token20. Both suffixes are exact prefixes of that same own-book formula. Literal English remains Through the same. Domine is a vocative; Mary is the third-person intercessor. The petition does not contain tuum/tuae/tibi or Thy/Thee. Father/Son address is established by the actual source cue and the table full wording Jesus Christ, Thy Son ... with Thee, plus the target Filium tuum/Qui tecum; no formula words are inserted into English.",
